/* book exam traps: Treating BiCMOS as plain CMOS plus one transistor. The buried layer, epitaxy and sinker are exactly what make the NPN fast, and what cost masks, yield and thermal budget. | Swapping buried layer and sinker. Both are n+; the buried layer is implanted before the epitaxy and lies under the device, the sinker is a deep implant from the surface down to it. | Assuming a higher β is always better. A thinner base raises β but lowers breakdown; lighter base doping raises β but raises base resistance. β is a design trade. | Getting the thermal order wrong. The buried layer goes first because epitaxy and well drive-in are hot; the shallow base goes late so it does not spread. */
