/* book exam traps: Using λ for both the layout unit and the lithography wavelength. In a layout question λ is the unit; the printer wavelength is a separate number in nm. | Confusing minimum width with minimum spacing. Width is one shape; spacing is the gap between two shapes. | Swapping enclosure and extension. Enclosure surrounds a shape on all sides; extension runs past an edge on one side only. | Computing pitch as width plus twice the spacing, or as width alone. Pitch is one width plus one spacing. | Mixing units halfway: a length in λ multiplied by λ in nm instead of μm, giving an answer off by 1000. */
